clean_summary:
Using DINOv3, especially when scaled up, reduces the performance gap with text-aligned vision encoders like CLIP when applied to vision-language models.

@oriane_simeoni: "Here is the summary slide presented yesterday. Using Molmo setup, encoder frozen and fine-tuning Qwen2-7B."

The key points are that scaling DINOv2 ViT-g to 1 million iterations on 1.7 billion images boosts performance, scaling to 7 billion images with gram and HRFT approaches closes the gap with text-aligned encoders, and distilled ViT-H+ performs as well as a 7 billion parameter model.

