I'm pretty excited about this. Tim Darcet is, in my opinion, a legend in modern self-supervised learning: he developed DINOv2, was involved in DINOv3, and invented ViT registers. He has a recent paper formulating a new SSL approach called CAPI, and he'll be presenting it in our journal club on Thursday.

At @MedARC_AI, we're very interested in exploring alternative SSL approaches beyond the standard DINO and MAE paradigms. We believe innovations in SSL training will lead to better medical imaging foundation models. So we're looking forward to learning more about CAPI, and we invite you to join us.

@MedARC_AI is hosting a journal club presentation on July 30th at 8:30am PT. @TimDarcet from Meta will present his paper "CAPI: Cluster and Predict Latent Patches for Improved Masked Image Modeling." Join the Discord and check our website.

